From 8f42413d70f09ce6c114443bc00a479e2ad54f52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jjude80 <18168364+jjude80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:22:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(opencode): recover agents from transient provider
 failures

The OpenCode adapter returned no machine-readable error class, so the
server's existing bounded-transient-retry path could never see an
opencode failure. A provider blip therefore left the agent row in error
with no next run and the card parked.

Classify failed attempts as provider_quota or transient_upstream, retry
transient transport blips in-run with bounded backoff, and keep the
agent idle only when a durable retry was actually queued. Non-transient
failures still end in error, and retry exhaustion stays visible.
